th giving it  back to her against my will the quest  had four optional objectives killing the  men in front of me  and then three different endings  delivering the heirloom to the woman  turning her in for blackmail or taking  the heirloom from myself which blew me  away with the amount of options that i  was given one thing that kept me  immersed in playing this dlc was the  original soundtrack it has around 60  tracks and music equating to about 3  hours of originally composed music it's  different yet similar to skyrim and that  the idea of what kind of composition  they made is similar but i got a  different tune to match the new area  we're in  cereal clearly has a different feel to  it than skyrim so the music should have  a different feeling and it absolutely  nails that the other element of keeping  the immersion was by far my favorite  which has got to be the voice acting  so many unique personalities and all of  them hit perfectly whether the dialogue  was serious or humorous  [Applause]  [Music]  while bruma would still be good if they  used generic voices or no voices at all  like some other mods it just wouldn't  feel the same as the acting makes the  world feel  real and it doesn't take you out of the  immersion it's a sometimes overlooked  detail but it pays off in the end if  done correctly  according to the credits there are 30  people who made up the voices for aruma  some of whom have some pretty large  credits in gaming such as dragon age  inquisition wasteland 2 and dying light  2.  this is just a taste of brooma and i  highly encourage you to try this mod for  yourself if you have the time i know  it's available on pc and from what i've  heard it might be available on console  but it might be a little hard to find  with the mod menus  if room is going to be a representation  of what the other counties will be like  in the future then i'm very excited to  see the full cereal release it's one of  the most expensive and unique dlc mods  i've played for skyrim in a very long  time and it's clear the devs care about  this mod and have put in the work to  make others like it too we then come to  our final mod which is end roll and as  we  said ender all is a game not a dlc like  bruma  full game and it's recognized as one on  steam as it comes up with its own  achievements and its own store page  and the requirements being the specs and  skyrim needs to be purchased  according to the developers it's roughly  a 30 to 100 hour run time which is  excellent for people looking for fresh  new original content but to keep that  skyrim feel would i be lying to you if i  said that this was skyrim with a new  story cause  it's not under all has certain similar  elements like the three bars at the  bottom and a  tree system but completely flipped most  of the other game's mechanics on its  head  off the start health does not regenerate  meaning you have to pick your fights  wisely and the only way to heal is by  eating food drinking a potion or  sleeping making eating and drinking food  actually really useful  enemies are a lot tougher i played on a  lower difficulty on ender all than i did  on skyrim and i was still getting my ass  beat  the term wolves are stronger in packs  was completely true as i found myself  sitting on top of hal's roofs just to  get away from a pack of them  i found myself also getting caught by  enemies wind-up tacks a lot more often  which instead of shaking my screen  slightly and moving me down a little bit  it actually stopped me from moving and  attacking altogether leaving me open for  more damage  magic and stamina are the two bars that  regenerate but in combat it's slower  than normal when it's out of combat  potions are your greatest ally but they  also aren't instantaneous they heal over  time  if food or potions are out then you can  use light magic which is the game's  restoration magic but  any source of healing in the game causes  arcane fever using too much healing  magic takes a strain on your body which  causes you to get a percentage of arcane  fever  too much and you start to lose some  stats and attributes other forms of  magic are fine to use it's just the  healing one to cure this arcane fever  you can either smoke some p-sweet to  calm the nerves or if you need to fix it  faster use some ambrosia but ambrosia  can cost you around 20 gold per bottle  so save some coins for it speaking of  that the skills have been renamed and  changed combat has now been split from  workmanship  most of these are pretty  self-explanatory but to explain the ones  that are a bit more complex to  understand simply psionics is illusion  magic elementarism is destruction magic  mentalism is alteration  entropy is conjuration and light magic  is restoration for the worksmanship tree  handicraft is smithing and rhetoric is  speech and barter these sounds simple  but of course these skills go very far  in depth and they're not just as simple  as a class of magic ranking these up  isn't as simple either instead of using  a specific action described in the skill  tree name enough times like hitting  somebody and leveling up your one-handed  leveling these up is only done by  finding books that are of the correct  proficiency than reading them these can  either be looted off people or bought  from various vendors so not only do you  need to keep gold for ambrosia but also  the books too for worksmanship books  they require the book and the available  crafting points and the combat tree  requires the book and available learning  points so if you want to increase your  two-handed skill from 15 to 16 you're  gonna need a learning book that is  labeled two-handed and then use a  learning point to read it but i can tell  you're a little bit curious as if we  can't level up skills how do we level up  and where do we get the points from well  it's just old-fashioned xp killing  enemies rewards xp just like any typical  rpg  once you level up you're in a set amount  of learning points and crafting points  and memory points per level  memory points are those skill points for  the skill trees this is done by using  the talent meditate in the talon tab of  magic which replaces the shouts which  then shoots you into this dream world  the base game has the three generic  trees but the new dlc forgotten stories  adds lycanthropy and phasmalist in  simple terms lycanthropy is the werewolf  and phasmalist is for soul gems and  enchanting  this is enderall's version of the skill  tree except way more interactive  you start from the bottom then go all  the way up to the top in any way you  choose just like normal but you're  actually in there in person picking the  skills for yourself most of the beginner  skills will give you talents which are  small buffs that last a short amount of  time  one of them boosted my one-handed damage  for seven seconds once that seven  seconds was up i could cast the talent  again with no negative effects so i was  constantly using it in multiple fights  the skill tree was a really cool  experience the first time being able to  walk around and look at the trees in  person like that was truly amazing  to exit simply meditate again and you're  back to where you started when you left  almost like you paused and went up to  the menus to level up and then back just  like in skyrim except more interactive  all of this represents the basics of  enderall's combat and i'm truly amazed  as i've mentioned constantly i still  cannot shake the habit of using a  one-handed heavy armor character but an  ender all took me a full 10 minutes to  make the switch almost immediately to a  full magic character  besides the magic just being fun to use  i needed to do as much damage as  possible while taking as little damage  as possible and archery and magic  allowed me to do that perfectly so i  opted for magic the thing that confused  me was that the map was actually pretty  small  close to dragonborn dlc size i was  expecting a much larger world until i  realized the next mechanic of ender all  is that there's no  waiting or traditional fast travel now  the game isn't trying to torture you  about this when entering the first city  called the ark you can fast travel to  the different districts within the city  by interacting with the signs  if you need to go to a specific town  there's most likely going to be a scroll  labeled for which you can use to  teleport to the location of the town  almost immediately  alternatively there's also going to be a  combo of spells the first one allows you  to place a marker anywhere on the map  with the second one being able to  teleport you to that marker no matter  where you are  for more true fast travel methods there  are the myriads which are located on the  maps as these towers  these towers house creatures that will  teleport you to other towers of course  if this is too bothersome for you there  are mods that exist out there that add  waiting and fast travel back into the  game but it's intended to be played  without it but before you get any of  this information you  have to go through the intro and might i  say it's a bit of an interesting one  my my i totally forgot what a mess i  left here  but i was right wasn't i a real gem  we've got here  bring me a nice crisp piece of meat  bring me a nice crisp piece of meat  bring me a nice crisp piece of meat like  i said  very interesting the game already is  just mesmerizing to look at on ultra  settings and the first area really  conveys that everything is more colorful  and vibrant compared to skyrim's bleak  and depressing world and the sound  design is top tier with the music being  some of the best i've heard in a game in  a while  and since we're on the topic let's  discuss the story i won't spoil any end  game missions simply the first couple  acts which can be done in about two to  three hours assuming you don't get  sidetracked the start  is you having this recurring nightmare  of your family claiming you killed them  that's the intro then you awake on a  ship with your partner  you are refugees fleeing a recent war  and snuck on a ship to start a new life  eventually you do end up being caught by  the captain your friend is killed and  you're thrown off the ship you arrive on  the beach somehow alive but before you  wake up you see these constant visions  none of it making sense  now but will make tons of sense as you  slowly understand what the visions mean  throughout the game  and depending on some of your future  choices you may be able to see these  visions in person  after some exploring talking with people  and more crazy visions you meet jess  barr one of the three companions of the  game and personally one of the best  voice acted characters i've ever  listened to i can't put my finger on it  but there's something strange about you  and that intrigues me what do you say he  is where the story truly starts as he  takes a journey along to assist you in  your troubles which leads you down a  rabbit hole of craziness as you start  piecing together information and  learning about the island's history  things like the high ones the cleansing  the light burns and the red madness all  things that sound very vague at face  value but end up being explained in time  as the more you progress through the  story the more you understand  jaspar is a good segue to companions as  the companions you can choose from after  some time will allow you to return the  favor and help them with their troubles  and companion quests  these do have a deadline so you can't  just put these off to the very end you  do have to do these relatively quickly  the whole point of these is to allow you  to interact with your companion more and  learn more about them it's a small  detail but a fantastic one at that  it's something i always wish skyrim  added to their companions now to be fair  they have a dozen or so companions so  maybe just the more important ones will  be getting quests there are a whole  bunch of other things about this game  that are unique from knowledge points  and magic symbols that appear in random  places that just make this whole  experience fantastic and if anything  this is the true fresh experience for  skyrim players  getting mods that change the base game  are cool and switching up current  strategies in the current game can help  as well but these are just small things  that'll only change up the pace for a  couple hours at most that's why i saved  bruma and enderall for last as these are  the very definition of a fresh new  experience one being a dlc which is part  of the main game and the other being a  whole unique  ip with very little brought over from  the game in terms of its mechanics both  of which serve the players in different  ways allowing them to have the true  fresh experience we've discussed many  mods  in this section and honestly i could  have brought up so many more as there's  just a plethora of mods that exist  all of them being very unique in their  own ways sadly we just don't have the  time but that being said though this is  the end of our journey and i thank you  for coming along with me everything  we've discussed i personally believe  are the answers to the question why is  skyrim a game that hasn't had a  significant update since 2016  still played after nine years for the  harmonizing music the iconic story the  nostalgic memories you've all made  across the years  all of it i believe is the answer to  that simple question hopefully you all  enjoyed this video i've got a bunch more  games to include in this series but i'm  bound to miss some so let me know what  you'd like me to cover in the future  after skyrim it's only fair our next  couple videos like this cover the other  great bethesda series and we'll be  starting that series with fallout 3.  as i stated before thank you for joining  me on this journey through the wondrous  world of the other skulls 5 skyrim and  i'll see you soon goodbye  [Music]  you
 

